y, they discover that the true value of toilet paper lies not in its absorbency, but in the bonds of humanity it can forge.  In the end, they must choose between survival and the greater good, facing a moral dilemma that could change the course of history.',	'poster_199.png',	'{"title":"Toilet Paper Apocalypse","runtime_mins":63,"genres":"Action, Comedy","rating":"2.4","released":2012,"actors":"Eric Wright","director":"Wong Pui Ying","plot":"In a world gripped by a global toilet paper shortage, a group of unlikely heroes must navigate a treacherous landscape of hoarding, black markets, and desperate bartering.  Their mission: to secure a precious stash of the coveted commodity and restore order to a society teetering on the brink of chaos.  But as they journey, they discover that the true value of toilet paper lies not in its absorbency, but in the bonds of humanity it can forge.  In the end, they must choose between survival and the greater good, facing a moral dilemma that could change the course of history."}'),
