, leaving the jury to decide not only the fate of the defendant but also the integrity of the justice system itself.  The film culminates in a dramatic courtroom showdown where the jury''s verdict becomes a powerful statement about the complexities of truth and justice.',	'poster_62.png',	'{"title":"The Jury Speaks","runtime_mins":69,"genres":"Thriller, Drama","rating":"4.7","released":2008,"actors":"Valentina Gómez,  Sarah Williams,  Julian Sanders","director":"Sophie Müller","plot":"A high-profile murder trial hinges on the testimony of a single witness, but the jury is deeply divided. As the deliberations drag on, tensions rise, and secrets are revealed, forcing the jurors to confront their own biases and prejudices.  A shocking twist exposes a hidden agenda within the courtroom, leaving the jury to decide not only the fate of the defendant but also the integrity of the justice system itself.  The film culminates in a dramatic courtroom showdown where the jury''s verdict becomes a powerful statement about the complexities of truth and justice."}'),
